### [QStringList](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qstringlist.html) QSettings::childGroups() const

Returns a list of all key top-level groups that contain keys that can be read using the
[QSettings](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qsettings.html) object.

Example:

```
QSettings settings;
settings.setValue("fridge/color", QColor(Qt::white));
settings.setValue("fridge/size", QSize(32, 96));
settings.setValue("sofa", true);
settings.setValue("tv", false);

QStringList groups = settings.childGroups();
// groups: ["fridge"]
```

If a group is set using
[beginGroup](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qsettings.html#beginGroup)(), the
first-level keys in that group are returned, without the group prefix.

```
settings.beginGroup("fridge");
groups = settings.childGroups();
// groups: []
```

You can navigate through the entire setting hierarchy using
[childKeys](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qsettings.html#childKeys)() and
childGroups() recursively.

**See also** [childKeys](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qsettings.html#childKeys)()
and [allKeys](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qsettings.html#allKeys)().

